### Summary

This paper proposes a method to generate synthetic data on the fly during training. The synthetic data is generated by a stable diffusion model. The method first generates a set of marginal samples from the training set, and then uses these samples to generate synthetic data. The generated synthetic data is then filtered by the variance of gradients. The authors show that the proposed method can improve the performance of a classification model.

### Soundness

2 fair

### Presentation

2 fair

### Contribution

2 fair

### Strengths

The idea of generating synthetic data on the fly is interesting.

### Weaknesses

1. The proposed method is not well motivated. The authors claim that the proposed method can improve the performance of a classification model. However, it is not clear how the proposed method can improve the performance. The authors only show that the proposed method can generate synthetic data that is close to the real data. However, it is not clear how this can improve the performance of a classification model. 

2. The proposed method is not well explained. The authors claim that the proposed method first generates a set of marginal samples from the training set, and then uses these samples to generate synthetic data. However, it is not clear how the marginal samples are generated. The authors claim that the marginal samples are generated by ranking the training samples based on the predicted probability of the training samples. However, it is not clear how the predicted probability is calculated. 

3. The proposed method is not well evaluated. The authors only show that the proposed method can improve the performance of a classification model on a few datasets. However, it is not clear how the proposed method performs on other datasets. The authors only show the performance of the proposed method on a few datasets, but do not provide any information about the performance of the proposed method on other datasets.

### Questions

1. What is the motivation of the proposed method? How can the proposed method improve the performance of a classification model?

