### Summary

This paper proposes a new parallel training method for reversible neural networks. The proposed method, PETRA, decouples the forward and backward passes in the training process, which allows for parallelizing the computation of the gradients across different devices. The authors demonstrate that the proposed method can achieve competitive accuracy with backpropagation on CIFAR-10, ImageNet-32, and ImageNet.

